      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T10:19:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we should really check CUR_IMG if it has a region that\nneeds preserving. NEW_IMG may not have the same preserve\nrequirements.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1741,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 1741,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09a43dac_c1d69085",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1741,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T11:23:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`dump_fmap \"${NEW_IMG}\" -e | grep -q \u0027 preserve\u0027`\n\nWe are running this command before doing read of EC flash, if there are any sections that needs to be preserved as per NEW_IMG, then we will do the flash read. Until we do this flash read, we don\u0027t know what is in EC chip image or CUR_IMG.\n\nOne thing I just realized is, if we use CUR_IMG `preserve` status to determine preserving in NEW_IMG, then we might need to do full flash read in almost all cases. Right now we don\u0027t do flash read if preserve status is not enabled in any sections of NEW_IMG.\n\nRight now the following commands doing the presence check of sections in CUR_IMG: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/util/flash_ec;l\u003d1763-1764\n\nWe could also avoid flash_ec script run failure by suppressing above error if we want to, but as it\u0027s better to break earlier than later, we are not suppressing them till now",
      "parentUuid": "29849fc0_3b587e49",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1741,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 1741,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84c2ae76_40d51b8e",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1741,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-28T06:05:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "checking the `preserve` flag in NEW_IMG instead of CUR_IMG means we don\u0027t\nrespect the existing `preserve` flag (see b/297804096). and yes, we do need\nto check if CUR_IMG has `preserve` regions now that we store persistent data\nthere. we need to address the performance penalty (b/288589393) for this to\nbe practical.\n\nwe do not need to suppress the error currently reported by flash_ec - it\u0027s a valid case that should not be treated as an error.",
      "parentUuid": "09a43dac_c1d69085",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1741,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 1741,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4203e0c4_454cce61",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T08:24:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s possible to do this way but we are using NEW_IMG so far because it tells/determines what\u0027s needed for it. We have node property called `preserve`, which tells a section should be preserved or not. If it\u0027s set to false it won\u0027t do the preserve.\n\nOne case this change could break is, if the CBI portion has `preserve` flag set false in CUR_IMG and set to true in NEW_IMG.  The general expectation is it needs to preserve or get the CBI data from CUR_IMG, but it won\u0027t with this change\n\nOther case would be, If CUR_IMG marked CBI as preserve, but in NEW_IMG it\u0027s marked as don\u0027t preserve and we have new CBI data in NEW_IMG, we could only flash it using --no_preserve tag to avoid preserving. But --no_preserve should not be required in this case as per device tree configuration in NEW_IMG\n\nWe need to use --no_preserve until we don\u0027t have CBI data present in the CUR_IMG. Without `no_preserve` it fails which also works as alert that the CBI section is not in-place. Generally --no_preserve is meant for factory use case to put initial CBI into device, similar to flashing EEPROM at factory, normally dev won\u0027t need this flag.\n\nThe flashing won\u0027t fail in the following case but it\u0027s expected to, CUR_IMG don\u0027t have CBI, but NEW_IMG (with `preserve` flag set to true) is expecting to get the CBI from CUR_IMG\n\nIt\u0027s also bit complicated for a new user to understand if the behavior relies on old image properties, instead of new image properties",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f46a5f88_2fdaaefb",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T09:03:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "using NEW_IMG doesn\u0027t make sense because that ignores the preserve flag\nin the existing image. more importantly, the implemented logic detects\na false failure when the existing image does not have a CBI region.\n\n`The general expectation is it needs to preserve or get the CBI data from CUR_IMG`\nthe preserve flag that needs to be respected is the one that describes\nthe bits at risk. using the preserved flag from the new image to infer\nthat bits in the old image should be preserved is strange. i don\u0027t\nthink setting the preserve bit in the new image should have precedent\nover the preserve bit in the old image. if we need to \"invalidate\"\nthe preserve setting in the old image, we should use the --no_preserve\nflag.\n\nwhat\u0027s complicated is that flash_ec now requires special attention to\ntransition a system from a flashmap without CBI to one with CBI and that\u0027s\nentirely avoidable.",
      "parentUuid": "4203e0c4_454cce61",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af35c58a_cdcc83af",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T09:37:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t use `no_preserve` often, it\u0027s only meant for first flash of CBI in EC flash. \n\nThe devices generally come with CBI in EC flash from factory. Consider `no_preserve` will not be used by us, until CBI is corrupted that came from factory\n\nNormally a EC dev won\u0027t face the case that is addressed here AFAIK i.e, the flash failing because CBI is not present in OLD_IMG, but the NEW_IMG trying to preserve it\n\nThe behavior of property `preserve` is inspired from binman: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/third_party/u-boot/+/4500973\n\nActually what we meant by (or my understanding of) preserve is, we won\u0027t use the sections that are marked `preserve`(in image with updates) from new binary, while updating all sections on flash. we continue using current version of the preserve sections, while others get updated\n\nBut in flash_ec case, we can\u0027t do flashing section wise, if it was possible we would have skipped flashing those sections based on NEW_IMG `preserve\u0027 flags, so we are copying the sections that marked as `preserve` in NEW_IMG from OLD_IMG, keeping other sections as it is in NEW_IMG\n\nIf I understood it correctly, I think the error coming up at flashing process when trying to preserve some sections from CUR_IMG which don\u0027t have them, is a valid error, cause it tells me the valid data not available in earlier version, instead of silently skipping copying, booting up and failing later with error \"Invalid CBI data\"",
      "parentUuid": "f46a5f88_2fdaaefb",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ec3a82e_f3e077f2",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T10:05:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this check both old and new and maybe require an explicit flag if there\u0027s some inconsistency?",
      "parentUuid": "af35c58a_cdcc83af",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d956cf49_d870cafd",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T10:19:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`But in flash_ec case, we can\u0027t do flashing section wise, if it was possible we would have skipped flashing those sections based on NEW_IMG`\n\nthere\u0027s no fundamental reason we can\u0027t. considering it takes\n2 minutes to read the flash right now to `preserve` 256 bytes of CBI,\nwe should seriously look into addressing that: find the flash map,\nextract CBI region, etc.. cbfstool can do it, so the information\nmust be there.\n\nagain, we should not use the preserve flag from NEW_IMG to describe\ndata in CUR_IMG as that negates the whole point of having a preserve\nflag in the on-device image.\n\n`I think the error coming up at flashing process when trying to preserve some sections from CUR_IMG which don\u0027t have them, is a valid error`\nbut that\u0027s the actual use case we\u0027re experiencing right now as we\u0027re\nadding a new region that needs to be preserved.",
      "parentUuid": "4ec3a82e_f3e077f2",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1070d82_37821fa3",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T11:03:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually there is an action item to look into optimization of flash read while preserving the protected sections, but I haven\u0027t started working on that yet\n\n\n`but that\u0027s the actual use case we\u0027re experiencing right now as we\u0027re\nadding a new region that needs to be preserved.`\n\nActually this should not happen in general use-cases, is it possible to share more info around what is the device and the scenario\n\n\nI am just putting the other way of what is preserve current behaviour again, the preserve status in an IMG will let it decide to use it\u0027s version or the previous version\n\nSo the preserve flag in CUR_IMG is not ignored, it\u0027s considered while it was a NEW_IMG\n\nBy default CBI is marked as `preserve`. So until someone voluntarily overrides that property in device tree, it won\u0027t stop preserving or through `no_preserve`",
      "parentUuid": "d956cf49_d870cafd",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
